## 4. NestJS Architecture

### File & Folder Structure

```
src/
  app/                        # AppModule
  common/
    constants/                # App-wide constants and env variable types
    db/                       # PrismaService, DbModule
    decorators/               # Shared decorators (e.g. @CurrentUser)
    interfaces/               # Shared interfaces (IApiResultResponse, IEntityResponse)
    utils/                    # Utilities (encryption, jwt, validators, treeBuilder)
  modules/
    <feature>/
      dto/                    # DTOs with class-validator decorators
      guards/                 # Feature-specific guards
      decorators/             # Feature-specific decorators
      constants/              # Feature constants (Prisma selects, table configs)
      <feature>.module.ts
      <feature>.service.ts
      <feature>.controller.ts          # REST controller
      <feature>.table.controller.ts    # Table/CRUD metadata controller (optional)
    public/
      controllers/            # Public API controllers (api-key authenticated)
      public-api.module.ts
  shared/
    tenant/                   # Tenant decorators and utilities
libs/
  logger/                     # market-logger library
prisma/
  schema/                     # Multi-file Prisma schema (one .prisma per model)
  migrations/                 # Migration SQL files
```

### Modules
ALWAYS export services that other modules need:

```typescript
@Module({
  controllers: [StrategyController],
  providers: [StrategyService],
  exports: [StrategyService],      // ✅ export if used by other modules
})
export class StrategyModule {}
```

### Dependency Injection
ALWAYS inject dependencies via constructor with `private readonly`:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
constructor(private readonly prismaService: PrismaService) {}

// ❌ BAD
@Inject(PrismaService) prismaService: PrismaService;
```

### Controllers
ALWAYS specify `version: '1'` and the full path in `@Controller`:

```typescript
@Controller({ path: 'strategies', version: '1' })
```

Public API controllers (api-key authenticated) go in `src/modules/public/controllers/` and use `path: 'public/<resource>'`.

### Guards & Scopes (Public API)
Public API controllers ALWAYS use both guards. Scope annotation is per-method:

```typescript
@Controller({ path: 'public/strategies', version: '1' })
@UseGuards(ApiKeyGuard, ApiKeyScopeGuard)
export class PublicStrategyController {
  @Get()
  @RequireApiKeyScopes('strategies:read')
  async list() { ... }

  @Post()
  @RequireApiKeyScopes('strategies:write')
  async create() { ... }
}
```

### Tenant Context
ALWAYS extract `projectId` via `@CurrentTenant()` decorator in public API controllers. NEVER read from request headers manually.

