## 5. Code Style & Formatting

### Response Shape
ALL controller methods MUST return `{ result: T }`:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — create
return { result: { id: entity.id.toString() } };

// ✅ GOOD — list
return { result: list };

// ✅ GOOD — update / delete / restore
return { result: true };

// ❌ BAD — raw return
return entity;
```

Use the shared interfaces: `IApiResultResponse<T>` and `ICreateEntityResponse`.

### Error Handling
USE NestJS HTTP exceptions. NEVER throw generic `Error`:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
throw new NotFoundException('Strategy not found');
throw new BadRequestException('Cannot update deleted strategy');
throw new UnauthorizedException('Invalid or expired API Key');

// ❌ BAD
throw new Error('not found');
```

### Soft Deletes
Entities with a `deleted` boolean field use soft deletes. NEVER hard-delete records. Use `deleted: true` to mark as deleted, `deleted: false` to restore. ALWAYS filter `deleted: false` in list queries by default.

### BigInt IDs
Prisma models use `BigInt` IDs. ALWAYS convert to `string` before returning from a controller:

```typescript
return { result: { id: record.id.toString() } };
```

### Logging
USE `private readonly logger = new Logger(ClassName.name)` inside classes. NEVER use `console.log`:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
private readonly logger = new Logger(ApiKeyGuard.name);
this.logger.debug('Processing...');
this.logger.error('Failed', error);

// ❌ BAD
console.log('Processing...');
```

### Formatting Rules (Prettier / ESLint)
- Single quotes for strings
- 2-space indentation
- Trailing commas everywhere
- Max line length: 200 characters
- Blank line required before `return`, `try`, `throw`, and block statements
- NEVER use `else` after a `return` statement (`no-else-return`)
- ALWAYS use object shorthand: `{ name }` not `{ name: name }`
- ALWAYS use strict equality: `===`, never `==`
- Imports MUST be sorted (`simple-import-sort` is enforced)

